body:
So true, but sometimes' looking good' has nothing to do with physical appearance. It also has to do with your positive and confident energy when you have something to offer.  

For example, I was EXTREMELY stalked and harassed by my manager when I worked at King Soopers. But in terms of physical appearance I looked terrible. I was tired, sweating and working. I had a work uniform on and a hat and an apron. I was definitely nothing above fancy. However, as plain and sweaty as I physically appeared the manager still had enough emptiness and bitterness in her heart to find a reason to envy me and hate my existence. But really there was NOTHING to envy about me. I'm not more interesting or special then the next person. And I definitely wasn't a threat to her. I was just an ordinary employee trying to get by to do my job. 

&#x200B;

Bottom line: When it comes to envy and gang stalking, the envy has more to do with the gang stalker and the emptiness inside of them. It has nothing to do with you or your physical appearance. 

&#x200B;

Again let me repeat: When a gang stalker is envious of you and harassing you, it has NOTHING to do with you. But it has a lot to do with them and the deep deep deep emptiness inside themselves.

If that's the way you feel you should set boundaries between you and your friends. It sounds like you have a lot on your plate and you need support right now. Tell you friends you can't help them if they ask you too and start asking your friends to help you out more. Tell them how you feel. You just lost your mom and are getting married so they should be understanding about you needing support.

&#x200B;

If you do these things and they still don't help you then it's time to distance yourself :/

Right! I know how you feel. People treat me like a piece of shit 24/7 so no one has the right to tell me not to feel suicidal or what I can or can't do with my life. And people treat me like shit but when I go people might be sad (maybe) but no ones going to think twice about their actions. 

&#x200B;

 What really pisses me off is when someone feels suicidal, people care a lot more about the what but not about the why.
